    ; key. Any other object is the receiver of the function: it is evaluated before the key, and
    ; a struct that lies in storage is read where the function is called, as the receiver of any
    ; call is, so it is what evaluating the key left there. Each takes the conversion recorded
    ; for it. A function that raises answers its value or an error, which leaves the function
    ; with the call where the type pass says so, as any call's does.
