    ; each argument of the tail, which `given` holds from `start` on, is converted to the list's
    ; item and appended to it by the call recorded at the argument. One with the bullet is
    ; appended only where it is present, as what it holds: an optional where it holds a value,
    ; and the tuple of a key and an optional value where the value holds one. Any other with
    ; the bullet has no shape yet.
